User Request:  
"During our next maintenance window, we need to implement BGP fast reroute capabilities specifically for IPv6 labeled-unicast traffic on our Nokia 7750 SR PE routers to maintain sub-second convergence times in case of path failures within the MPLS core, particularly where dual-stack services are carrying sensitive real-time applications—what's the most efficient way to configure this while ensuring it doesn't impact existing IPv4 FRR policies?"

