User Request:  
During a recent network optimization project, we're looking to streamline our Nokia 7750 SR router's performance by ensuring only relevant routes populate the routing table manager and forwarding information base. What would be the recommended approach to suppress the automatic installation of all BGP-learned routes in the base router instance while maintaining proper route advertisement capabilities?

Retrieved Reference Content (from the configuration manual):  
{
    "PageTitle": "ignore-router-id",
    "FuncDef": "When theignore-router-idcommand is present, and the current best path to a destination was learned from EBGP peer X with BGP identifier x and a new path is received from EBGP peer Y with BGP identifier y, the best path remains unchanged if the new path is equivalent to the current best path up to the BGP identifier comparison - even if y is less than x.",
    "CLIs": [
        "ignore-router-id include-internal <family> [ <family> ]",
        "[ no ] ignore-router-id"
    ],
    "ParentView": [
        "config>router>bgp>best-path-selection",
        "config>service>vprn>bgp>best-path-selection"
    ],
    "ParaDef": [
        {
            "Parameters": "family",
            "Info": "Specifies up to two internal families to be included in this configuration. Values-mvpn-ipv4, mvpn-ipv6."
        }
    ],
    "Examples": null,
    "ExtraInfo": "Default: no ignore-router-id"
}
{
    "PageTitle": "advertise-inactive",
    "FuncDef": "This command enables the advertising of inactive BGP routes to other BGP peers. By default, BGP only advertises BGP routes to other BGP peers if a given BGP route is chosen by the route table manager as the most preferred route within the system and is active in the forwarding plane. This command allows system administrators to advertise a BGP route even though it is not the most preferred route within the system for a given destination.",
    "CLIs": [
        "advertise-inactive",
        "no advertise-inactive"
    ],
    "ParentView": [
        "config>router>bgp",
        "config>router>bgp>group",
        "config>router>bgp>group>neighbor"
    ],
    "ParaDef": null,
    "Examples": null,
    "ExtraInfo": "Default: no advertise-inactive"
}
{
    "PageTitle": "mp-bgp-keep",
    "FuncDef": "As a result of enabling this command, route refresh messages are no longer needed, or issued when VPN route policy changes are made; RIB-IN will retain all MP-BGP routes.",
    "CLIs": [
        "mp-bgp-keep",
        "no mp-bgp-keep"
    ],
    "ParentView": [
        "config>router>bgp"
    ],
    "ParaDef": null,
    "Examples": null,
    "ExtraInfo": "Default: no mp-bgp-keep"
}
{
