"During a recent core network upgrade, we're implementing BGP on our Nokia 7750 SR 7750 routers and need to ensure session stability during transient link failures—what's the recommended approach to adjust BGP timers or damping mechanisms so neighbor relationships aren't immediately dropped when OSPF detects a brief interface flap?"

