User Request:  
During a multi-site core network upgrade, we need to implement BGP route reflection with redundancy safeguards for our Nokia 7750 SR routers—specifically, one of the reflector groups requires a cluster ID of 192.168.10.5 while ensuring optimal exit path selection via ORR location 8, even if primary routes become unavailable. What’s the recommended configuration approach to enforce this hierarchy while maintaining local fallback capabilities in case of upstream failures?

