To enforce immediate BGP session teardown when the path to a neighbor becomes unavailable, configure peer tracking globally under BGP:

```cli
configure router bgp
    enable-peer-tracking
exit
```

This ensures sessions terminate immediately upon loss of the underlying route without waiting for hold timer expiration. For granular control, apply the command at the group or neighbor level:

```cli
configure router bgp group "GROUP_NAME"
    enable-peer-tracking
exit
```

```cli
configure router bgp group "GROUP_NAME" neighbor "IP_ADDRESS"
    enable-peer-tracking
exit
