To ensure BGP sessions terminate immediately when the underlying route becomes unavailable, enable BGP peer tracking. This accelerates failover by dropping peers instantly upon route removal without waiting for the hold timer. Apply the following configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp
    enable-peer-tracking
```

This command can also be configured per group or neighbor if granular control is required. For example:
```cli
configure router bgp group "GROUP_NAME"
    enable-peer-tracking
```
```cli
configure router bgp group "GROUP_NAME" neighbor "PEER_IP"
    enable-peer-tracking
```
