To enable IPv4 unicast address family support for receiving link-bandwidth extended communities from eBGP peers on your Nokia 7750 SR router, apply the following CLI configuration:

```console
configure router bgp
    group "EBGP_GROUP_NAME"
        link-bandwidth
            accept-from-ebgp ipv4
        exit
    exit
exit
```

**Key elements:**
- `accept-from-ebgp ipv4` enables processing of link-bandwidth attributes from eBGP peers for IPv4 unicast routes
- This configuration must be applied under the relevant BGP group or neighbor context
- The router will now use received link-bandwidth data for traffic engineering decisions

For unequal-cost load balancing scenarios where you'll re-advertise routes with `next-hop-self`, also include:
```console
aggregate-used-paths ipv4
```
This aggregates bandwidth values from multipaths when advertising to peers.
