During a maintenance window to enhance network stability, I need to ensure uninterrupted forwarding for IPv6 traffic flows even if the routing protocol restarts. Could you guide me through setting up persistent graceful restart capabilities specifically for the IPv6 address family on our Nokia 7750 SR platform? We want to minimize any potential disruption during control plane transitions.

Retrieved Reference Content (from the configuration manual):  
{
    "PageTitle": "stale-routes-time",
    "FuncDef": "This command configures the maximum amount of time in seconds that stale routes should be maintained after a graceful restart is initiated.",
    "CLIs": [
        "stale-routes-time <time>",
        "no stale-routes-time"
    ],
    "ParentView": [
        "config>router>bgp>graceful-restart",
        "config>router>bgp>group>graceful-restart",
        "config>router>bgp>group>neighbor>graceful-restart"
    ],
    "ParaDef": [
        {
            "Parameters": "time",
            "Info": "Specifies the amount of time that stale routes should be maintained after a graceful restart is initiated. Values-1 to 3600 seconds."
        }
    ],
    "Examples": null,
    "ExtraInfo": "Default: no stale-routes-time"
}
{
    "PageTitle": "enable-notification",
    "FuncDef": "When this command is present, the graceful restart capability sent by this router indicates support for NOTIFICATION messages. If the peer also supports this capability then the session can be restarted gracefully (while preserving forwarding) if either peer needs to sends a NOTIFICATION message due to some type of event or error.",
    "CLIs": [
        "enable-notification",
        "no enable-notification"
    ],
    "ParentView": [
        "config>router>bgp>graceful-restart",
        "config>router>bgp>group>graceful-restart",
        "config>router>bgp>group>neighbor>graceful-restart"
    ],
    "ParaDef": null,
    "Examples": null,
    "ExtraInfo": "Default: no enable-notification"
}
{
    "PageTitle": "restart-time",
    "FuncDef": "This command sets the value of the restart-time that is advertised in the router s graceful-restart capability. If this command is not configured, the default is 300.",
    "CLIs": [
        "restart-time <seconds>",
        "no restart-time"
    ],
    "ParentView": [
        "config>router>bgp>graceful-restart",
        "config>router>bgp>group>graceful-restart",
        "config>router>bgp>group>neighbor>graceful-restart"
    ],
    "ParaDef": [
        {
            "Parameters": "seconds",
            "Info": "Specifies the restart-time that is advertised in the router s graceful-restart capability. Values-0 to 4095 seconds. ParamDefault: Default- config>router>bgp>graceful-restart: 120 secondsconfig>router>bgp>group>graceful-restart: 300 secondsconfig>router>bgp>group>neighbor>graceful-restart: 300 seconds"
        }
    ],
    "Examples": null,
    "ExtraInfo": "Default: no restart time"
}
{
    "PageTitle": "backup-path",
    "FuncDef": "This command enables the computation and use of a backup path for IPv4 and/or IPv6 BGP-learned prefixes belonging to the base router. Multiple paths must be received for a prefix in order to take advantage of this feature. When a prefix has a backup path and its primary paths fail, the affected traffic is rapidly diverted to the backup path without waiting for control plane re-convergence to occur. When many prefixes share the same primary paths, and in some cases also the same backup path, the time to failover traffic to the backup path is independent of the number of prefixes.",
    "CLIs": [
        "backup-path [ ipv4 ] [ ipv6 ] [ label-ipv4 ] [ label-ipv6 ]",
        "no backup-path [ ipv4 ] [ ipv6 ] [ label-ipv4 ] [ label-ipv6 ]"
    ],
    "ParentView": [
        "config>router>bgp"
    ],
    "ParaDef": [
        {
            "Parameters": "ipv4",
            "Info": "Enables BGP fast reroute for unlabeled unicast IPv4 routes."
        },
        {
            "Parameters": "ipv6",
            "Info": "Enables BGP fast reroute for unlabeled unicast IPv6 routes."
        },
        {
            "Parameters": "label-ipv4",
            "Info": "Enables BGP fast reroute for labeled-unicast IPv4 routes."
        },
        {
            "Parameters": "label-ipv6",
            "Info": "Enables BGP fast reroute for labeled-unicast IPv6 routes."
        }
    ],
    "Examples": null,
    "ExtraInfo": "Default: no backup-path"
}
{
    "PageTitle": "forwarding-bits-set",
    "FuncDef": "This command determines the setting of the F bits in the GR and LLGR capabilities advertised by the router. When the F bit is set for an AFI/SAFI, it indicates that the advertising router was able to preserve forwarding state for the routes of that AFI/SAFI across the last restart. If a router restarts and does not set F=1, then when the session with a peer re-establishes the peer immediately deletes all LLGR stale routes it was preserving on behalf of the restarting router for the corresponding AFI/SAFI.",
    "CLIs": [
        "forwarding-bits-set { all | non-fwd }",
        "no forwarding-bits-set"
    ],
    "ParentView": [
        "config>router>bgp>graceful-restart>long-lived",
        "config>router>bgp>group>graceful-restart>long-lived",
        "config>router>bgp>group>neighbor>graceful-restart>long-lived"
    ],
    "ParaDef": [
        {
            "Parameters": "all",
            "Info": "Specifies that the F bit for all AFI/SAFI should be set to 1."
        },
        {
            "Parameters": "non-fwd",
            "Info": "Specifies that the F bit for only non-forwarding AFI/SAFI should be set to 1. These AFI/SAFI correspond to the following families: L2-VPN, route-target, flow-IPv4, and flow-IPv6."
        }
    ],
    "Examples": null,
    "ExtraInfo": "Default: no forwarding-bits-set"
}
{
    "PageTitle": "graceful-restart",
    "FuncDef": "This command enables BGP graceful restart helper procedures (the \"receiving router\" role defined in the standard) for address families included in the GR capabilities of both peers. SR OS can support GR helper functionality for IPv4, IPv6, VPN-IPv4, VPN-IPv6, Label-IPv4, Label-IPv6, L2-VPN, Route-Target (RTC), Flow-IPv4 (IPv4 flow-spec) and Flow-IPv6 (IPv6 flow-spec) routes.",
    "CLIs": [
        "graceful-restart",
        "no graceful-restart"
    ],
    "ParentView": [
        "config>router>bgp",
        "config>router>bgp>group",
        "config>router>bgp>group>neighbor"
    ],
    "ParaDef": null,
    "Examples": null,
    "ExtraInfo": "Default: no graceful-restart"
}

