"During a recent core network upgrade, we need to ensure uninterrupted IPv6 traffic forwarding while neighboring routers reboot. Could you outline the necessary steps to configure BGP graceful restart helper support specifically for IPv6 prefixes on our Huawei NE40E platform, maintaining existing sessions during the maintenance window?"

```cli
configure router bgp next-hop-resolution
    labeled-routes
        transport-tunnel
            family label-ipv4
                resolution-filter
                    bgp
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

This configuration enables BGP tunneling for next-hop resolution of labeled IPv4 routes. The key elements are:
- Targets `label-ipv4` address family specifically for labeled IPv4 prefixes
- Uses `bgp` tunnel type under `resolution-filter` to resolve next-hops via BGP label-unicast IPv4 tunnels
- Maintains separation from VPN/vpn-ipv4 route resolution
- Leaves existing unlabeled IPv4/IPv6 and VPN resolution unchanged

The hierarchy navigates through:
`bgp > next-hop-resolution > labeled-routes > transport-tunnel > family label-ipv4 > resolution-filter`

This ensures BGP-created tunnels (/32 IPv4 prefixes) are used exclusively for resolving next-hops of labeled IPv4 routes without impacting other address families or tunnel types.
