Based on your requirement to ensure reliable BGP next-hop resolution for labeled and VPN prefixes using static routes without default routes, apply the following configuration:

```cli
configure router
    bgp
        enable-rr-vpn-forwarding
        next-hop-resolution
            labeled-routes
                allow-static
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

**Explanation:**  
- `enable-rr-vpn-forwarding` enables VPN route resolution via a dummy VRF, allowing static routes to resolve VPN next-hops.  
- `allow-static` under `labeled-routes` permits non-default static routes to resolve next-hops for both labeled-unicast (IPv4/IPv6) and VPN prefixes.  

This configuration excludes default static routes (`0/0` or `::/0`) while ensuring all other static routes are considered for next-hop resolution.
