## User question:
When setting up BGP Monitoring Protocol on our Nokia 7750 SRs, we need to adjust the session establishment parameters — specifically, what would be the recommended approach to modify the connection retry interval to accommodate longer convergence times during maintenance windows, increasing it from the default to a 5-minute threshold?
---
## Proposed answer:
To adjust the BGP connection retry interval to 5 minutes (300 seconds) for accommodating longer convergence times during maintenance windows, use the following CLI command:

```console
configure router bgp
    connect-retry 300
```

This command modifies the BGP connect retry timer globally. To apply it to a specific group or neighbor, navigate to the respective configuration context:

**Group-level configuration:**
```console
configure router bgp group <group-name>
    connect-retry 300
```

**Neighbor-level configuration:**
```console
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address>
    connect-retry 300
---
