To ensure VPNv4 prefixes propagate over IPv6 transport with IPv6 next-hop addresses on Nokia 7750 SR routers, configure the following BGP commands:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group <IPV6_PEER_GROUP>
        family vpn-ipv4
        advertise-ipv6-next-hops vpn-ipv4
        extended-nh-encoding vpn-ipv4
        neighbor <PEER_IPV6_ADDRESS>
            peer-as <AS_NUMBER>
        exit
    exit
exit
```

**Key configuration details:**  
1. **`advertise-ipv6-next-hops vpn-ipv4`**  
   Forces VPNv4 routes to use IPv6 next-hops when advertised over IPv6 transport sessions.

2. **`extended-nh-encoding vpn-ipv4`**  
   Advertises BGP capability to handle IPv6 next-hops for VPNv4 routes, required for compatibility with IPv6 peers.

3. **`family vpn-ipv4`**  
   Maintains VPNv4 route exchange capability simultaneously with IPv6 transport.

**Verification commands:**  
```cli
show router bgp neighbor <PEER_IPV6_ADDRESS> advertised-routes family vpn-ipv4
show router bgp neighbor <PEER_IPV6_ADDRESS> received-routes family vpn-ipv4
```

**Important considerations:**  
- Apply this configuration only to IPv6 peer groups/neighbors to avoid impacting existing IPv4 transport sessions  
- Ensure matching `extended-nh-encoding vpn-ipv4` exists on all participating BGP peers  
- IPv4-based customer VRFs remain unaffected as this only modifies BGP transport behavior
------------
