To ensure your Nokia 7750 SR routers properly utilize aggregated bandwidth from EBGP neighbors for incoming IPv4 routes using link-bandwidth extended communities, apply the following CLI configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group "EBGP_GROUP"
        link-bandwidth
            accept-from-ebgp ipv4
            aggregate-used-paths ipv4
```

### Explanation:
1. **`link-bandwidth`**: Enters the configuration context for handling link-bandwidth extended communities under the BGP group.
2. **`accept-from-ebgp ipv4`**: Allows the router to accept and process link-bandwidth extended communities attached to IPv4 routes received from EBGP peers.
3. **`aggregate-used-paths ipv4`**: Combines bandwidth metrics from all active multipaths for IPv4 prefixes when re-advertising routes with `next-hop-self`, enabling effective utilization of consolidated link bandwidth.

Apply this configuration to all relevant BGP groups or neighbors where EBGP peering exists. Ensure multipath BGP is properly configured to leverage path aggregation.
