## User question:
"During a recent core network upgrade involving Nokia 7750 SR routers, we encountered a situation where BGP path selection was inadvertently influenced by IGP metrics for next-hop reachability when evaluating identical NLRIs from our primary BGP peers. What's the proper method to modify the route comparison logic so it disregards the resolved IGP distance while maintaining all other BGP best path selection criteria?"
---
## Proposed answer:
To modify BGP path selection to ignore IGP metrics for next-hop reachability while preserving other criteria, use this command:

```
configure router bgp best-path-selection ignore-nh-metric
```

This command disables IGP distance consideration during BGP best-path selection without affecting other attributes like AS path length, origin type, MED, or local preference.
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
ignore-nh-metric
no ignore-nh-metric
FuncDef:
This command instructs BGP to disregard the resolved distance to the BGP next-hop in its decision process for selecting the best route to a destination. When configured in theconfig>router>bgp>best-path-selectioncontext, this command applies to the comparison of two BGP routes with the same NLRI learned from base router BGP peers. When configured in theconfig>service>vprncontext, this command applies to the comparison of two BGP-VPN routes for the same IP prefix imported into the VPRN from the base router BGP instance. When configured in theconfig>service>vprn>bgp>best-path-selectioncontext, this command applies to the comparison of two BGP routes for the same IP prefix learned from VPRN BGP peers.
ParaDef:
No ParaDef found
