To modify BGP path selection to strictly adhere to BGP attributes and ignore IGP metrics to next-hop addresses, use the following configuration:

```
configure router bgp best-path-selection ignore-nh-metric
```

This command disables the inclusion of resolved IGP distance in the BGP decision process for identical NLRIs. Path selection will now exclusively follow standard BGP attribute comparisons (e.g., weight, LOCAL_PREF, AS_PATH length).
