To ensure graceful restarts without triggering unnecessary route withdrawals during maintenance, configure the following BGP settings on your Nokia 7750 SR router. These commands enable helper functionality, preserve forwarding state, and maintain stale routes during peer restarts:

```cli
configure router bgp
    graceful-restart
    stale-routes-time 300
    enable-notification
    no shutdown
exit
```

**Key configuration details:**  
1. **`graceful-restart`**: Enables helper mode to preserve neighbor adjacencies and forwarding state during peer restarts.  
2. **`stale-routes-time 300`**: Maintains stale routes for 300 seconds (adjustable) to prevent immediate route flushing when peers reboot.  
3. **`enable-notification`**: Allows graceful session recovery even if peers send NOTIFICATION messages during restarts.  

> **Note**:  
> - Apply these commands globally under `bgp` to cover all peers, or target specific groups/neighbors using `group <name>` or `neighbor <ip>` contexts if needed.  
> - The `stale-routes-time` value (default: unset) should exceed your expected peer reboot duration (max 3600 seconds).  
> - No `restart-time` adjustment is required on helper routers—peers advertise their own restart timers during GR negotiations.
------------
