During routine BGP peering maintenance on a Huawei NE40E router, we've noticed instances where our local AS appears in the received AS_PATH from an established neighbor. Given our security policy mandates quietly dropping these potentially problematic routes while maintaining session stability, what's the recommended approach to implement this selective route filtering without disrupting existing BGP adjacencies?

configure router bgp
