To resolve the BGP next-hop resolution issues for labeled IPv4 routes in your MPLS-based transport network, configure BGP tunneling under the labeled routes context:

```cli
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        labeled-routes
            transport-tunnel
                family ipv4
                    resolution-filter
                        bgp
                    exit
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

This configuration enables BGP tunneling (BGP-LU) for next-hop resolution of labeled IPv4 routes while preserving existing label distribution policies. The `bgp` command under `resolution-filter` allows BGP label-unicast IPv4 routes to resolve next-hops via /32 IPv4 prefix tunnels.
