To ensure seamless BGP session preservation during NOTIFICATION exchanges and handle unplanned interruptions without route flaps, configure the following at the BGP group level:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        graceful-restart
            enable-notification
        exit
    exit
exit
```

**Key details:**  
- `graceful-restart` enables BGP session preservation during restarts.  
- `enable-notification` explicitly allows graceful handling of NOTIFICATION messages.  

This configuration:  
1. Preserves forwarding states during unplanned interruptions.  
2. Prevents route flapping by maintaining sessions during NOTIFICATION exchanges.  
3. Requires peer routers to support the same graceful restart capabilities.  

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP peer group name. Apply this to all relevant BGP groups participating in the maintenance.
