To implement a locally enforced stale time of one hour (3600 seconds) and disregard the remote endpoint's advertised LLGR value, use the following CLI configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp
    graceful-restart
        long-lived
            helper-override-stale-time 3600
        exit
    exit
exit
```

### Key details:
1. **`helper-override-stale-time 3600`** overrides the peer's advertised LLGR timer with a locally enforced value of 3600 seconds (1 hour).
2. Configured globally under `graceful-restart > long-lived` to apply to all peers.
3. The command forces the router to use the local timer value (3600 seconds) instead of the remote peer's advertised LLGR stale time.

This ensures consistent route withdrawal handling while ignoring remote LLGR timer advertisements.
