```

**Explanation:**  
- `purge-timer 60` sets the global BGP stale route purge interval to **60 minutes** (matching the 1-hour LLGR window).  
- `stale-routes-time 3600` enforces **local retention of stale routes for 3600 seconds (1 hour)** during restarts.  
- `advertised-stale-time 3600` advertises the **1-hour LLGR stale time** to all peers in BGP capabilities.  
- `helper-override-stale-time 3600` **overrides peer-advertised LLGR stale times** with the local 1-hour setting when acting as a helper.  

This configuration ensures consistent 1-hour LLGR behavior across all scenarios (local restarts/peer restarts) while maintaining routing stability through coordinated timers.
