Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.

To ensure uninterrupted forwarding for IPv6 traffic during routing protocol restarts on your Nokia 7750 SR, configure BGP graceful restart with the following commands:

```cli
/configure router bgp
    graceful-restart
        restart-time 300
        stale-routes-time 600
        enable-notification
    exit
```

This configuration:
- Enables BGP graceful restart globally
- Sets the maximum route preservation time to 600 seconds (10 minutes)
- Advertises a 300-second (5-minute) restart timer to peers
- Allows graceful session restart after NOTIFICATION messages

IPv6 traffic flows will maintain forwarding during control plane transitions as the router preserves stale routes and negotiates restart capabilities with peers.
------------
As a network device expert, please determine whether the following answer correctly responds to the user's question based on the router configuration manual. Only output "Correct" or "Incorrect" without any explanation or additional information. You must make your own judgment based on the Router configuration manual provided to you, not on your own knowledge.
---
## User question:
During a maintenance window to enhance network stability, I need to ensure uninterrupted forwarding for IPv6 traffic flows even if the routing protocol restarts. Could you guide me through setting up persistent graceful restart capabilities specifically for the IPv6 address family on our Nokia 7750 SR platform? We want to minimize any potential disruption during control plane transitions.
---
## Proposed answer:
To ensure uninterrupted forwarding for IPv6 traffic during routing protocol restarts on your Nokia 7750 SR, configure BGP graceful restart with the following commands:

```cli
/configure router bgp
    graceful-restart
        restart-time 300
        stale-routes-time 600
        enable-notification
    exit
```

This configuration:
- Enables BGP graceful restart globally
- Sets the maximum route preservation time to 600 seconds (10 minutes)
- Advertises a 300-second (5-minute) restart timer to peers
- Allows graceful session restart after NOTIFICATION messages

IPv6 traffic flows will maintain forwarding during control plane transitions as the router preserves stale routes and negotiates restart capabilities with peers.
