To adjust BGP flowspec validation settings on your Nokia 7750 SR router, use the following CLI commands. Configure these settings within the `flowspec` context under BGP:

### Enable Flowspec Validations:
```cli
configure router
    bgp
        flowspec
            validate-redirect-ip
            validate-dest-prefix
```

### Disable Flowspec Validations:
```cli
configure router
    bgp
        flowspec
            no validate-redirect-ip
            no validate-dest-prefix
```

### Key Details:
- **`validate-redirect-ip`**: Enables validation of the `redirect-to-IPv4` action in received flowspec routes.
- **`validate-dest-prefix`**: Enables validation of flowspec routes containing destination-prefix subcomponents.
- Both settings are configured under `config>router>bgp>flowspec`.
- Use `no <command>` to revert to the default disabled state (`no validate-redirect-ip`/`no validate-dest-prefix`).
