To address the issue of orphaned VPN-IPv4 and VPN-IPv6 routes not being processed due to missing VPRN associations, use the following configuration:

```cli
configure router
    bgp
        enable-rr-vpn-forwarding
        next-hop-resolution
            labeled-routes
                transport-tunnel
                    family vpn
                    exit
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

### Key actions performed:
1. **`enable-rr-vpn-forwarding`**:  
   Imports all received VPN-IP routes into a dummy VRF for BGP next-hop resolution, regardless of route targets. This ensures orphaned VPN routes are processed.

2. **`family vpn` under transport tunnels**:  
   Configures next-hop resolution specifically for VPN-IPv4/VPN-IPv6 routes lacking VPRN associations. This enables proper handling of next-hops using eligible transport tunnels.

This setup maintains forwarding correctness by ensuring next-hops are resolved through supported transport tunnels while excluding unsupported methods like SR policies for VPN routes.
