## User question:
During a recent core network upgrade, we're planning to leverage BGP-LS for improved traffic engineering visibility across our Nokia 7750 SR routers – could you walk me through the specific configuration steps required to properly activate link-state data propagation into the BGP-LS tables? I need to ensure we maintain accurate topology information for our SDN controller integration.
---
## Proposed answer:
To activate BGP-LS for link-state data propagation on your Nokia 7750 SR routers, use the following CLI configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp
    link-state-import-enable
```

This command enables the import of IGP link-state information into the BGP-LS address family, allowing topology data to be advertised to BGP neighbors (including your SDN controller). Ensure your BGP neighbors are properly configured for the link-state address family to propagate this data.
