To implement multipath advertisement and negotiation for unlabeled IPv4 prefixes with up to eight paths per destination on Nokia 7750 SR routers, use the following BGP add-paths configuration. Apply this at the neighbor or group level for the transit provider peer:

```cli
configure router bgp
  group "TRANSIT_PROVIDER_GROUP"
    neighbor <IP_ADDRESS>
      add-paths
        ipv4 send 8 receive
      exit
    exit
  exit
exit
```

**Key details:**  
- `ipv4 send 8` enables advertising up to 8 best paths per unlabeled IPv4 prefix  
- `receive` allows accepting multiple paths from the peer for the same prefix  
- This configuration is backward compatible; add-paths capability is negotiated only with supporting peers  
- Replace `TRANSIT_PROVIDER_GROUP` and `<IP_ADDRESS>` with your specific group and neighbor IP  

For global application to all IPv4 peers (if preferred):  
```cli
configure router bgp
  add-paths
    ipv4 send 8 receive
  exit
exit
```
