To enable multipath support for unlabeled IPv6 prefixes with up to 8 paths in a dual-stack BGP peering setup, use the following configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <neighbor-ip>
            family ipv6
            add-paths
                ipv6 send 8 receive
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

**Key details:**
- The `ipv6 send 8 receive` command under `add-paths` enables both sending and receiving of up to 8 unlabeled IPv6 paths per prefix.
- This is configured at the neighbor level for granular control but can also be applied at the group or global BGP level.
- Ensure `family ipv6` is enabled on the neighbor to activate IPv6 peering.

For IPv4 unlabeled prefixes (if required in your dual-stack setup), apply the corresponding configuration:
```cli
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <neighbor-ip>
            family ipv4
            add-paths
                ipv4 send 8 receive
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```
