## User question:
When configuring BGP-based tunnels on our Nokia 7750 SR routers for improved traffic engineering, we need to ensure proper path selection by leveraging entropy labels—how should this capability be enabled to maintain optimal load balancing across the MPLS infrastructure without disrupting existing LSPs?
---
## Proposed answer:
To enable entropy label capability for BGP-based tunnels and ensure optimal load balancing without disrupting existing LSPs, use the following configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp
    override-tunnel-elc
    exit
```

This command activates entropy labels on BGP tunnels, improving load distribution across the MPLS infrastructure while preserving current LSP operations.
