To temporarily advertise suboptimal BGP routes during migration, configure BGP multipathing to allow multiple paths and adjust best-path selection to prioritize route stability. Use these CLI commands:

```cli
configure router bgp
   multipath 2
   best-path-selection
      ignore-router-id
   exit
exit
```

**Explanation:**  
- `multipath 2` enables installation of multiple paths per prefix (up to 2), allowing suboptimal routes to be used locally for failover.  
- `ignore-router-id` retains existing best paths during route updates, preventing unnecessary route flapping when new suboptimal paths are received.  

This ensures alternative routes remain active and propagated while maintaining connectivity during legacy equipment phase-out. Revert to default settings (`no multipath`, `no ignore-router-id`) after migration completes.
