To achieve optimal path diversity while limiting advertised multipath routes to eight per mVPNv4 prefix and maintaining the ability to accept multiple multicast routes, apply this BGP configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp
    add-paths
        mvpn-ipv4 send 8 receive
    exit
exit
```

### Key details:
1. **`mvpn-ipv4 send 8`**  
   Restricts advertised multipath routes to a maximum of 8 paths per mVPNv4 prefix.

2. **`receive`**  
   Maintains the capability to accept multiple multicast routes per prefix from peers.

This configuration balances path diversity control with scalability requirements for multicast VPN deployments. Apply it globally under BGP, or selectively at the group/neighbor level as needed.
