To ensure uninterrupted IPv6 traffic forwarding during neighboring router reboots via BGP graceful restart helper support on your Nokia 7750 SR, configure the following:

```config router bgp
graceful-restart
    restart-time 300
exit
```

### Key details:
- **`graceful-restart`**: Enables helper functionality to preserve IPv4/IPv6 routes (including labeled and unlabeled IPv6) during neighbor restarts.
- **`restart-time 300`**: Sets the maximum wait time for neighbor re-establishment to 300 seconds (default is 120 globally), matching typical maintenance windows.

This configuration:
1. Preserves IPv6 forwarding paths while neighbors reboot.
2. Uses standard BGP graceful restart procedures for all supported IPv6 address families (unicast and labeled-unicast).
3. Applies globally to all BGP peers; no IPv6-specific commands are needed as IPv6 support is inherent. 

For neighbor-specific tuning (e.g., per-peer timers), apply the same commands under `group` or `neighbor` contexts.
