## User question:
During a recent network upgrade, we noticed that our Nokia 7750 SR routers aren't initiating TCP keepalives promptly enough to detect stale connections in our high-availability environment—could you adjust the idle timer so the first probe gets sent after five minutes of inactivity? We want to maintain session persistence while ensuring timely failure detection.
---
## Proposed answer:
To adjust the TCP keepalive idle timer to send the first probe after five minutes of inactivity, use the following commands. Replace `<station-name>` with your BMP station name:

```cli
configure
    bmp
        station <station-name>
            connection
                tcp-keepalive
                    keep-idle 300
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
