Your answer:

To adjust the BGP hold timer to 60 seconds and set the corresponding keepalive interval on your Nokia 7750 SR routers, use the following commands. These can be applied globally, per group, or per neighbor:

### For a specific neighbor:
```cli
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <neighbor-IP> hold-time 60 min 60
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <neighbor-IP> keepalive 20
```

### For an entire BGP group:
```cli
configure router bgp group <group-name> hold-time 60 min 60
configure router bgp group <group-name> keepalive 20
```

### Globally for all BGP peers:
```cli
configure router bgp hold-time 60 min 60
configure router bgp keepalive 20
```

### Key details:
1. **`hold-time 60 min 60`**  
   - Sets the hold timer to 60 seconds and enforces a minimum of 60 seconds (rejects sessions requesting lower values).

2. **`keepalive 20`**  
   - Sets the keepalive interval to 20 seconds (standard practice: one-third of the hold timer).

Replace `<group-name>` and `<neighbor-IP>` with your specific BGP group and neighbor IP. After configuration, reset BGP sessions to apply the changes immediately.
