To ensure routers discard routes with an "Invalid" RPKI origin validation state during path selection, apply the following configuration:

```
configure router
    bgp
        best-path-selection
            origin-invalid-unusable
```

This command marks all routes with an "Invalid" RPKI origin state as unusable, excluding them from the best-path algorithm and preventing their use for forwarding or advertisement. This approach operates independently of existing policies and requires no modifications to them. Ensure RPKI validation is already enabled on relevant peers to generate the "Invalid" state.
