This configuration disables add-paths for labeled IPv4 routes globally. If applied at the group or neighbor level (e.g., `config>router>bgp>group>add-paths` or `config>router>bgp>group>neighbor>add-paths`), use the same `no label-ipv4` command under those contexts for specific peers. For other address families (e.g., IPv4, IPv6), repeat this pattern with their respective add-paths commands (e.g., `no ipv4`, `no ipv6`) if enabled.
