## Proposed answer:
```
configure router bgp
group <group_name>
neighbor <neighbor_ip>
family ipv6
prefix-limit ipv6 5000 threshold 80 log-only
exit
exit
exit
```

**Explanation:**  
- `prefix-limit ipv6 5000` sets the IPv6 route limit to 5000  
- `threshold 80` triggers a syslog warning at 4000 routes (80% of 5000)  
- `log-only` ensures only warnings are logged without session termination  
- Applied under neighbor/group IPv6 family configuration context  

**Verification:**  
After configuration, monitor syslog for warnings when routes reach 4000/5000. Session remains operational regardless of route volume. Adjust `<group_name>` and `<neighbor_ip>` to target specific peers.
