To adjust the BGP session stability parameters as requested, use the following CLI configuration commands:

```cli
configure router bgp
    keepalive 120
    hold-time 180 min 180
    damp-peer-oscillations idle-hold-time 1 2 10 error-interval 10
exit
```

### Explanation:
- **`keepalive 120`**: Sets the BGP keepalive interval to 120 seconds (2 minutes).
- **`hold-time 180 min 180`**: Configures the hold-time to 180 seconds (3 minutes) and ensures the peer must accept a minimum hold-time of 180 seconds. This accommodates neighbor response delays up to 60 seconds (`180s hold-time - 120s keepalive = 60s delay tolerance`).
- **`damp-peer-oscillations idle-hold-time 1 2 10 error-interval 10`**: Implements graceful fallback by:
  - Setting initial idle time after a session reset to **1 minute**.
  - Doubling the idle time to **2 minutes** for subsequent resets within the error interval.
  - Capping maximum idle time at **10 minutes**.
  - Requiring a **10-minute error-free period** to reset the penalty counter.
