To activate RibApi-programmed tunnels for next-hop resolution of label-IPv4 routes while maintaining existing MPLS forwarding performance, use the following CLI configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        labeled-routes
            transport-tunnel
                family label-ipv4
                    resolution-filter
                        rib-api
                    exit
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

This configuration:
1. Enters the BGP next-hop resolution context for labeled routes
2. Specifies the transport tunnel family for label-IPv4 routes
3. Adds RibApi to the resolution filter while preserving existing tunnel types (like RSVP/LDP)
4. Ensures RibApi-programmed tunnels are considered for next-hop resolution without affecting current MPLS forwarding

Existing tunnel types remain operational in the resolution filter, maintaining forwarding performance during the integration.
------------
