## Proposed answer:
To configure BGP for labeled IPv6 unicast and multicast VPN traffic on your Nokia 7750 SR routers while preserving existing IPv4 peerings, use the following CLI commands. Replace `<group-name>` and `<existing-families>` with your current BGP group and enabled address families (e.g., `ipv4`, `vpn-ipv4`). 

```cli
configure router
    bgp
        group <group-name>
            family <existing-families> label-ipv6 mvpn-ipv4 mvpn-ipv6
        exit
    exit
exit
```

### Key details:
- **`label-ipv6`**: Enables labeled IPv6 unicast routes.
- **`mvpn-ipv4`** and **`mvpn-ipv6`**: Enable multicast VPN for IPv4 and IPv6 services.
- **Preserving IPv4**: The `<existing-families>` must include all currently configured families (e.g., `ipv4`) to avoid disrupting peerings. 

### Verification:
After applying, confirm the new families are active:
```cli
show router bgp neighbor <ip-address> family
```

This approach adds the required IPv6 and multicast VPN capabilities without affecting existing IPv4 BGP sessions.
