## User question:
When deploying labeled-unicast BGP in our Nokia 7750 SR infrastructure, we need to ensure proper path selection during route redistribution. Could you advise on adjusting the administrative distance—specifically setting it to 150—for these L3VPN transport routes to deprioritize them compared to our core IGP? We're implementing this as part of the new edge POP rollout where we want the MP-BGP routes to remain as backup paths unless explicitly preferred.
---
## Proposed answer:
To adjust path selection for labeled-unicast BGP routes and deprioritize them compared to the core IGP, enable BGP fast reroute for labeled-unicast IPv4 and IPv6 routes to designate them as backup paths. Use the following CLI configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp
    backup-path label-ipv4 label-ipv6
