## User question:
During a recent network upgrade where we're implementing segment routing across our core, I need to ensure our Nokia 7750 SR routers properly propagate locally defined SR policies to all BGP neighbors that have been configured with the SR Policy AFI. What's the correct procedure to make these custom policies visible in BGP updates without affecting existing prefix advertisements?
---
## Proposed answer:
To ensure your Nokia 7750 SR routers propagate locally defined SR policies to BGP neighbors configured with the SR Policy AFI (AFI 1/SAFI 73), enable the import of static SR policies into BGP. Use the following CLI command:

```cli
configure router bgp sr-policy-import
```

This command imports statically configured non-local SR policies into the BGP RIB, allowing them to be advertised as originated routes to all BGP peers supporting the SR Policy address family. Existing prefix advertisements remain unaffected as this action is specific to the SR Policy AFI/SAFI.
