The cleanup of stale VPN-IP routes after a Route-Refresh request is controlled by the `purge-timer` setting. The default purge-timer is 10 minutes, and routes are removed when this timer expires. The purge-timer starts immediately after sending the Route-Refresh and does not include additional processing delays beyond the configured timer value.

To adjust the purge interval to 5 minutes (for example), use:
```cli
configure router bgp
    purge-timer 5
```
