To ensure seamless interoperability and prevent next-hop modification for labeled unicast routes (IPv4 and IPv6) when propagating to a designated peer group, use the following CLI configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp group <peer-group-name> third-party-nexthop
configure router bgp group <peer-group-name> extended-nh-encoding label-ipv4
```

### Explanation:
1. **`third-party-nexthop`**:  
   Prevents the router from modifying the BGP next-hop attribute when advertising labeled IPv4/IPv6 routes to EBGP peers in the same subnet. This maintains the original next-hop, avoiding unexpected AS_PATH prepending in route reflectors.

2. **`extended-nh-encoding label-ipv4`**:  
   Advertises the capability to handle extended next-hop encoding for labeled IPv4 routes (AFI=1/SAFI=4), ensuring compatibility when exchanging labeled unicast routes with peers.

Replace `<peer-group-name>` with your designated peer group. For IPv6 labeled unicast routes, ensure the transport address family matches the route family (implicitly handled by `third-party-nexthop`).
