```console
configure
    bmp
        station "monitoring-station"
            connection
                tcp-keepalive
                    keep-idle 300
                    keep-interval 30
                    keep-count 5
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

This configuration:
- Sets the initial idle period to **300 seconds** before sending the first keepalive probe
- Configures subsequent keepalive probes every **30 seconds**
- Declares the connection down after **5 consecutive missed keepalives**
- Balances stability (longer intervals) with failure detection (moderate retry threshold)
- Minimizes control plane load by reducing probe frequency versus default settings

Adjust `"monitoring-station"` to match your specific BMP station name. The values optimize between connection persistence (300s idle timer) and timely failure detection (30s probes + 5 retries = 150s failure window) while reducing overhead versus default settings.
