To prevent iBGP-learned routes from being reflected back to their originators on Nokia 7750 SR routers, enable the `split-horizon` feature. This ensures routes are not propagated back to the peer that initially advertised them. Apply the following configuration at the global BGP level:

```cli
configure router bgp
    split-horizon
exit
```

**Explanation:**  
The `split-horizon` command prevents the router from reflecting routes back to the peer that originally advertised them. It applies to all peer types (iBGP, eBGP, confed-eBGP) and address families, making it ideal for route reflector deployments. This configuration stops inadvertent route loops while maintaining normal propagation to other peers.  

**Alternative Scenarios:**  
If you need to apply this selectively to specific groups or neighbors, use:  
```cli
configure router bgp group <group-name>
    split-horizon
exit
```  
or  
```cli
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address>
    split-horizon
exit
```
