To configure BMP sessions for your primary and backup collectors on the Nokia 7750 SR, use these CLI commands:

```cli
/configure
    bmp
        station "NYC-DC1"
            connection
                router <router-instance-for-NYC>
            exit
        exit
        station "LAX-DC2"
            connection
                router <router-instance-for-LAX>
            exit
        exit
    exit
    router bgp
        monitor
            station "NYC-DC1" "LAX-DC2"
            route-monitoring pre-policy post-policy
        exit
    exit
```

**Key details:**
1. Replace `<router-instance-for-NYC>` and `<router-instance-for-LAX>` with your actual routing instances or VPRN service names
2. `route-monitoring pre-policy post-policy` enables both raw BGP updates (pre-policy) and policy-processed routes (post-policy)
3. Stations inherit the global BGP instance unless overridden in the station-specific `connection` context

For transport reliability:
- Ensure TCP port 1790 is open between routers and collectors (default BMP port)
- Verify routing instances have proper reachability to collector IPs
- Monitor sessions using `show router bgp bmp` operational commands
