To ensure uninterrupted BGP operation during maintenance, especially when handling malformed UPDATE messages where NLRI fields remain parsable, configure the following:

```console
configure router bgp
    error-handling
        update-fault-tolerance
    exit
```

**Key behavior:**  
- This enables `treat-as-withdraw` for non-critical UPDATE errors, preserving the session and valid routes when NLRI fields are correctly parsed despite other formatting issues.  
- Invalid routes in malformed messages are silently discarded instead of triggering session resets.  

**Note:** Apply this at the global BGP level (shown above), group level (`config>router>bgp>group>error-handling`), or neighbor level (`config>router>bgp>group>neighbor>error-handling`) as needed for granular control.
