```console
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        labeled-routes
            transport-tunnel
                family ipv4
                    resolution-filter sr-isis
                exit
                family ipv6
                    resolution-filter sr-isis
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

**Explanation:**  
This configuration enables IS-IS-learned SR tunnels for BGP next-hop resolution of **labeled IPv4/IPv6 routes**. The `resolution-filter sr-isis` command under the `labeled-routes > transport-tunnel > family` hierarchy ensures:  
1. BGP uses IS-IS-programmed SR tunnels for resolving next-hops  
2. Optimal forwarding paths are maintained by leveraging ISIS-calculated segments  
3. Supports both IPv4 and IPv6 labeled unicast prefixes  

The tunnel selection follows:  
- Lowest-preference IS-IS instance → Lowest-numbered IS-IS instance (per reference)  
- Automatically prefers SR tunnels over legacy protocols when installed in TTM
