Based on your requirement to prioritize SR tunnels from the least preferred OSPF instance for BGP next-hop resolution, configure the following CLI commands. This ensures BGP selects tunnels based on the highest numerical preference value (least preferred) across OSPF instances, with lower instance IDs breaking ties:

```cli
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        shortcut-tunn
            family ipv4
                resolution-filter sr-ospf
            exit
            family ipv6
                resolution-filter sr-ospf3
            exit
        exit
        labeled-routes
            transport-tunnel
                family ipv4
                    resolution-filter sr-ospf
                exit
                family ipv6
                    resolution-filter sr-ospf3
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

**Key Implementation Notes:**  
1. The `sr-ospf` (IPv4) and `sr-ospf3` (IPv6) resolution filters explicitly prioritize OSPF-advertised SR tunnels  
2. BGP automatically selects tunnels from the OSPF instance with the **highest numerical preference value** (least preferred). If preferences match, the lowest instance ID is chosen  
3. All other tunnel types (e.g., RSVP, SR-TE, SR-ISIS) are excluded to enforce OSPF SR tunnel prioritization  
4. Configured under both `shortcut-tunn` (unlabeled routes) and `labeled-routes` (labeled routes) for comprehensive coverage  

This configuration modifies only the BGP next-hop resolution behavior. Existing OSPF instance preferences and BGP routing policies remain unchanged.
